DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/day-of-the-dead-celebrations-
 day-3\n\nDay of the Dead Celebrations | Lecture by Rubí Tsanda Huerta\n\n
 Rubí is an internationally recognized writer\, poet\, historian\, Indigen
 ous interpreter\, and emerging actress from the P’urhépecha community o
 f Santo Tomás in the municipality of Chilchota\, Michoacán. She is the a
 uthor of three bilingual poetry collections in Spanish and P’urhépecha.
  Her most recent publication appeared in the anthology La voluntad de la t
 ierra\, edited by UNAM and the Instituto Cervantes de España.\n\nRubí wi
 ll be hosted at the Stanford Humanities Center and will lead a series of e
 vents in the context of the Day of the Dead.\n\nNov 2\, 2pm: What do altar
 s and dead mean for P’urhépecha communities? Intimate conversation with
  students and members of the Queer Student Resource Center.\n\nNov 3\, 4-5
 pm: Conversation and Blessing with El Centro students.\n\nNov 5\, 5–6:30
  pm: Lecture\, Dead and Life Celebrations in P’urhépecha Communities at
  the Native American Cultural Center.
END:VEVENT
